    {
      "name": "U.S. Telecommunications Mass Breach & Global Telecom and Infrastructure Targeting",
      "year_published": "2024",
      "description": "Salt Typhoon infiltrated at least nine major U.S. telecom providers (Verizon, AT&T, T-Mobile, Spectrum, Lumen, Consolidated Communications, Windstream) over one to two years. Compromised CALEA lawful intercept systems, accessing surveillance target lists, call content, text messages, and metadata on 1M+ users including senior government officials. Verizon and AT&T announced containment in December 2024. FBI Director Wray stated the group could not be fully expelled from most systems. White House established Cyber UCG on October 8, 2024. Congress approved $3B to remove Chinese equipment from U.S. telecom networks.\nBeyond U.S. targets, Salt Typhoon has infiltrated telecoms in over 80 countries and several dozen were compromised. Targets include government agencies, hotels, transportation, and military infrastructure worldwide. ESET documented hotel and government breaches globally. In November 2025, Australia's ASIO confirmed targeting of Australian telecom networks. A Canadian telecom was breached in February 2025. Viasat (U.S. satellite telecom) was named as a victim in June 2025.\n",
